# V2 (fixed) - the same requests as V1, with the correct outcomes.
# Use the REST Client extension in VS Code, or Rider/Visual Studio's .http support.

@host = http://localhost:5082
@orderId = paste-an-order-id-here

### List orders
GET {{host}}/api/orders

### 201 - Premium order (10% discount, 8% tax)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com", "tier": "Premium" },
  "items": [
    { "sku": "KB-01", "name": "Mechanical keyboard", "unitPrice": 120, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### 201 - the same name, now a SQL parameter
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "O'Brien", "email": "obrien@example.com", "tier": "Premium" },
  "items": [
    { "sku": "KB-01", "name": "Mechanical keyboard", "unitPrice": 120, "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### 400 - unknown tier is rejected at the boundary
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Goldie", "email": "gold@example.com", "tier": "Gold" },
  "items": [
    { "sku": "CH-01", "name": "USB-C cable", "unitPrice": 100, "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 400 - item validation (quantity must be 1..100)
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Ada Lovelace", "email": "ada@example.com", "tier": "Premium" },
  "items": [
    { "sku": "KB-01", "name": "Mechanical keyboard", "unitPrice": 120, "quantity": 0 }
  ]
}

### 200 - refund works: the order is an aggregate, not a lying subclass
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/refund

### 200 with DueOnDelivery - an honest payment contract
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "cod" }

### 409 - cancel twice: the aggregate enforces the state machine
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel

### 200 - card payment (Captured)
POST {{host}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/pay
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "card" }

### Sales report (depends on IOrderRepository only)
GET {{host}}/api/reports/sales
